      "note": "The block's ONE committed body: transaction ids, then transactions, then prune entries - the field order, which is also the normative leaf order for utxoTxRoot. These are byte-for-byte the tree inside orderingBlock/full, so a moved element byte fails here AND inside the framing rather than only in one of the two. An empty utxoTx is a bare zero length, which is what the lp prefix on that section exists for. The prune entry is the one element writer whose width varies. 'prune' and 'utxotx' are the only leaf domains under this root, and 'coinbase' and 'subblock' are RESERVED - never reuse either, since a leaf domain sits inside a consensus preimage."
